$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for synthesis of
bisquinoline compounds (3a-i). To a solution of ethyl
2-(halogenmethyl)quinoline-3-carboxylate 4 (1 mmol) in 15 mL CH3CN was
added 8-hydroxy quinolines 5 (1 mmol) and anhydrous potassium carbonate
(4 mmol). The resulting mixture was heated at reflux for 4 h. The
conversion was monitored by TLC. After completion, CH3CN was evaporated
to dryness and 10 mL water was added to the mixture. The resulting
precipitate was collected by filtration and purified by recrystallization
from ethanol to give products 3. Ethyl
2-((quinolin-8-yloxy)methyl)benzo[h]quinoline-3-carboxylate (3g); Yield:
86%; Brown solid. M.p. 219-220°C; IR (KBr, ν, cm-1): 2978, 2927, 2361,
1716 (C═O), 1596, 1566, 1499, 1378, 1315, 1246, 1105, 930, 816, 790, 747,
664; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) (δ, ppm): 1.42 (t, 3H, J = 7.2 Hz, CH2CH3),
4.41 (q, 2H, J = 7.2 Hz, CH2CH3), 6.50 (s, 2H, CH2), 7.38-7.54 (m, 1H,
Ar-H), 7.65 (t, 3H, J = 6.0 Hz, Ar-H), 7.68-7.73 (m, 5H, Ar-H), 7.75 (s,
1H, Ar-H), 7.82-7.91 (m, 1H, Ar-H), 8.18 (d, 1H, J = 8.4 Hz, Ar-H), 8.48
(d, 1H, J = 8.40 Hz, Ar-H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ (ppm): 14.17,
61.41, 71.04, 110.06, 119.76, 121.83, 124.31, 124.85, 125.27, 125.55,
126.85, 127.40, 128.20, 128.59, 129.16, 129.31, 130.10, 134.23, 135.86,
139.55, 139.89, 145.84, 148.96, 154.46, 154.81, 167.22. HRMS (ESI): m/z
[M + H]+ Calcd for C26H21N2O3+: 409.4029, found 409.4024.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Williamson ether synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A facile synthesis of bisquinoline derivatives via the Williamson
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gao, Wentao; Li, Yang; Wang, Songtao
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Research on Chemical Intermediates (2014), 40(2), 669-679

