$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
4-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-7-(2-oxopropoxy)-2H-2-chromenone (7). A hot solution
of 5 (1.07 g, 4 mmole) in absolute acetone (30 mL) was treated with
freshly calcined potash (1.66 g, 12 mmole), stirred vigorously and heated
(50-56°C), and treated with chloroacetone (0.35 mL, 4.4 mmole). The
reaction mixture was left for 1 h with heating and vigorous stirring
(completion of the reaction determined by TLC). The reaction mixture was
poured into H2SO4 solution (300 mL, I N). The resulting precipitate was
filtered off and crystallized from propan-2-ol.
7-[2-(4-Chlorophenyl)-2-oxoethoxy]-4-(4-methoxyphenyl)-2H-2-chromenone
(21). Prepared analogously to 7 from 5 (1.07 g, 4 mmole) and
4-chlorophenacylchloride (0.79 g, 4.2 mmole). Yield 1.45 g (86%).
C24H17ClO5, mp 202-203°C. IR spectrum (KBr, cm-1): 1710, 1694, 1617,
1514, 1419, 1383, 1293, 1252,1220,1181,1162,1125,1088, 1036,1010,985,
826. UV spectrum (CH3CN, λmax, nm, log ε): 203 (4.67), 252 (4.41), 313
(4.38). PMR spectrum (400 MHz, DMSO-d6, δ, ppm, J/Hz): 3.84 (3H, s,
OMe-4'), 5.75 (1H, s, CH2-1"), 6.20 (1H, s, H-3), 7.01 (1H, dd, J = 2.4,
J = 9.2, H-6), 7.11 (2H, d, J = BA, H-3', H-5'), 7.19 (1H, d, J = 2.4,
H-8), 7.43 (1H, d, J = 9.2, H-5), 7.50 (2H, d, J = 8.4, H-2', H-6'), 7.67
(2H, d, J = 8.4, H-3'", H-5'"), 8.05 (2H, d, J = 8.4, H-2'", H-6'").
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
