$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Allyl 1,1,7-trihydropefluoroheptyl ether (V).
To a solution of 3.88 g (0.069 mol) of potassium hydroxide in 13.6 ml
(0.072 mol) of 1,1,7-trihydroperfluoroheptanol (III), 55 ml of dioxane
was added, and the resulting solution was heated at 70-80°C with stirring
for 40 min. Water, 0.2 ml, was then added dropwise, the solution was
heated for an additional 30 min, after which 0.069 mol of allyl bromide
(or allyl iodide) was added. The reaction mixture was stirred at 60-70°C
for 20 min and then cooled to 30°C. The precipitate that formed was
filtered off. The mother liquor was diluted with 60 ml of water, and the
phases that formed were separated. The heavy phase was distilled to
obtain ether V, yield 84% (with allyl iodide). Transparent colorless
liquid, yield 84% (with allyl iodide). bp 97.5°C (38 mm Hg), d420 1.5279,
nD25 1.3300.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Williamson ether synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of allyl ethers derived from polyfluorinated alcohols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Rakhimov, A. I.; Shurubtsova, E. V.; Storozhakova, N. A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
