$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 4,5-Dibromo-3-methoxythiophene-2-carboxylate (11). To a solution
of 600 mg (1.9 mmol) of 10 in 7 mL of DMF were successively added 2.62 g
(19 mmol) of K2CO3 and then 200 μL (4.8 mmol) of MeI. After the mixture
was stirred for 12 h at room temperature, it was acidified with a
solution of HCl (1 M) to give a precipitate. The solid was filtered and
then was washed twice with water. The crude product was purified by
recrystallization in MeOH to give 520 mg of 11 (83% yield) as a beige
solid. mp = 76 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3): 3.87 (s, 3H), 4.02 (s, 3H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3): 52.3, 62.7, 112.9, 117.3, 117.5, 158.2, 160.0. MS (EI): 328
(M+•).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Williamson reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Electrogenerated Low Band Gap Polymers Based on the
3-Cyano-4-methoxythiophene Building Block
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
