$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General method for the synthesis of 2-aryloxy-N,N-diethyletanamine
hydrochlorides. A mixture of 0.1 mole of the corresponding phenol. 70 ml
toluene, 0.1 mole of hydrochloride or hydrobromide (2-chloro- or
2-bromo-, respectively) of N,N-diethylethanamine, and 12.5 g of
comminuted NaOH was boiled with stirring for 8 h on a sand bath, cooled,
alkalized with a NaOH solution until obtaining an alkaline reaction, and
extracted with ether (150 ml). The ether - toluene extract was washed
with NaOH solution until complete discoloration of the aqueous phase. The
organic layer was dried over crystalline NaOH and filtered. The filtrate
was purged with dry HCl and the precipitated
2-aryloxy-N,N-diethyletanamine hydrochloride was separated by filtration,
washed with ether, and crystallized from an appropriate solvent. In cases
where no solvent for crystallization can be found, the product is
purified by converting it onto the base form and repeated purging with
dry HCl. Compound I, yield 81.8%. Empirical formula: C12H19NO.HCl; M.p.
135 - 136°C (acetone); 1H NMR δ, ppm (CDCl3): 1.37 t (6H, N(CH2CH3)2),
3.01 - 3.40 m (6H, CH2N(CH2CH3)2), 4.40 t (2H, OCH2CH2), 6.63 - 7.25 m
(4H, arom. H), 12.20 bs (1H, NH+)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Williamson reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and antimicrobial activity of 2-aryloxy-N,N-diethylethanamine
derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Semenovykh, E. V.; Pantsurkin, V. I.; Novikova, V. V.; Odegova, T. F.;
Syropyatov, B. Ya.; Vakhrin, M. I.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Pharmaceutical Chemistry Journal (2007), 41(4), 211-215

