$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Aldehydes VI-IX (general procedure). A mixture
of 10 mmol of 5-chloromethyl-3-methyl-1,2-isoxazole (I), 10 mmol of
hydroxybenzaldehyde II-V, and 5 mmol of anhydrous potassium carbonate in
50 ml of 96% ethanol was heated for 12 h at 70°C under stirring in a
nitrogen atmosphere. The mixture was cooled and diluted with 100 ml of
water, and the precipitate was filtered off through a glass frit, washed
with water, and dried for 2-3 days at 25-30°C in air.
4-Methoxy-3-[(3-methyl-1,2-oxazol-5-yl)methoxy]benzaldehyde (VII). Yield
81%. mp 89-90°C. IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 3133 (CHisox); 3080, 3065, 3045,
3031, 3009 (CHarom); 2971, 2835, 2900, 2851, 2840 (CHaliph); 2761
(CHald); 1686 (C═O); 1615, 1597, 1583, 1509 (C═Carom); 1436 (C═Nisox);
1267, 1238, 1161, 1128, 1016 (C-O); 887, 831, 815, 805, 765, 740
(δCHarom). 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 2.27 s (3H, Me), 3.93 s (3H, MeO),
5.20 s (2H, CH2), 6.20 s (1H, 4'-H), 6.99 d (1H, Harom, 3J = 8 Hz), 7.44
s (1H, Harom), 7.50 d.d (1H, Harom, 3J = 8 Hz), 9.81 s (1H, CHO). 13C NMR
spectrum, δC, ppm: 11.50 (Me), 56.33 (OCH3), 62.19 (CH2), 104.65 (C4'),
111.30 (CHarom), 112.19 (CHarom), 127.71 (CHarom); 130.03, 147.84,
155.18, 159.99, 166.91 (Cquat); 190.66 (C═O). Mass spectrum: m/z 247
[M]+. Found, %: C 63.59; H 5.45; N 5.31. C13H13NO4. Calculated, %: C
63.15; H 5.30; N 5.67. M 247.25.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
