$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(4-Iodophenoxy)-N,N-diethylethanamine hydrochloride (XXXI). A mixture
of 12.32 g (0.056 mole) of 4-iodophenol, 40 ml toluene, 9.63 g (0.056
mole) of 2-chloro-N,N-diethyletanamine hydrochloride, and 7 g of
comminuted NaOH in a two-neck flask equipped with a mechanical stirrer
and a thermometer was heated with stirring for 14 h on a sand bath (so
that the temperature would not exceed 130°C), cooled, alkalized with a
NaOH solution until obtaining an alkaline reaction, and extracted with
ether (150 ml). The target hydrochloride was obtained as described above
for 2-aryloxy derivatives I - XXX. Yield 15.9 g, 79.9%. Empirical
formula: C12H18INO.HCl; M.p. 155 - 156°C (toluene); 1H NMR δ, ppm
(CDCl3): 1.430 t (6H, N(CH2CH3)2), 3.084 - 3.376 m (6H, CH2N(CH2CH3)2),
4.401 t (2H, OCH2CH2), 6.506 - 7.466 m (4H, arom. H), 12.3 bs (1H, NH+)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Williamson reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and antimicrobial activity of 2-aryloxy-N,N-diethylethanamine
derivatives
