$DATUM 4-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-7-(2-oxopropoxy)-2H-2-chromenone (7). A hot solution
of 5 (1.07 g, 4 mmole) in absolute acetone (30 mL) was treated with
freshly calcined potash (1.66 g, 12 mmole), stirred vigorously and heated
(50-56°C), and treated with chloroacetone (0.35 mL, 4.4 mmole). The
reaction mixture was left for 1 h with heating and vigorous stirring
(completion of the reaction determined by TLC). The reaction mixture was
poured into H2SO4 solution (300 mL, I N). The resulting precipitate was
filtered off and crystallized from propan-2-ol. Yield 1.01 g (78%).
C19H16O5, mp 151-152°C. IR spectrum (KBr, cm-1): 1733, 1715, 1608, 1517,
1419, 1377, 1305, 1281, 1267, 1249, 1185, 1150, 1116, 1067, 1029, 1005,
843. UVspectrum(CH3CN, λmax, nm, logs): 203 (4.91), 313 (4.35).
PMRspectrum (400MHz, DMSO-d6, δ, ppm, J/Hz): 2.18 (3H, s, CH3-3"), 3.84
(3H, s, OMe-4'), 5.00 (2H, s, CH2-1"), 6.19 (1H, s, H-3), 6.93 (1H, dd, J
= 2.4, J = 9.2, H-6), 7.05 (1H, d, J = 2.4, H-8), 7.12 (2H, d, J = 8.4,
H-3', H-5'), 7.42 (1H, d, J = 9.2, H-5), 7.49 (2H, d, J = 8.4, H-2',
H-6').
