$DATUM 3-(Benzyloxy)-5-[(1S,2R)-2-(2-ethoxyethyl)cyclopropyl]pyridine (16).
Compound 111 (0.42 g, 1.55 mmol) was dissolved in anhydrous DMF (10 mL),
cooled to 4 °C with the aid of an external ice-bath, and NaH (0.074 g,
3.1 mmol) was then added. After stirring for 10 min, iodoethane (0.48 g,
3.1 mmol) was added slowly. The reaction was further stirred at 4 °C for
20 min and allowed to warm to rt with continuous stirring overnight. The
reaction was quenched with aqueous NH4Cl, extracted with EtOAc (2x15 mL),
and the combined organic extracts were washed successively with water (10
mL) and brine (10 mL). The organic solution was dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4, concentrated under reduced pressure and purified by column
chromatography (silica gel) using CH2Cl2:CH3OH (90:10) as eluent to
obtain the desired product 16. Colorless oil, yield 0.36 g (78.3%). 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 8.15 (d, J = 2.8 Hz, 1H), 8.04 (d, J = 1.6 Hz,
1H), 7.43‒7.32 (m, 5H), 6.85 (t, J = 2.4, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 5.07 (s, 2H),
3.54‒3.46 (m, 4H), 1.67‒1.64 (m, 3H), 1.20 (t, J = 7.2, 6.8 Hz, 3H),
1.14‒1.08 (m, 1H), 0.94‒0.83 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 155.1,
141.3, 140.3, 136.5, 135.0, 128.9, 128.4, 127.8, 118.8, 70.5, 70.3, 66.5,
34.6, 21.0, 20.5, 15.8, 15.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Williamson ether synthesis
