$DATUM Ketones 11-24. A hot solution of coumarins 5-10 (4 mmol) in anhydrous
acetone (30 mL) was treated with freshly calcined potash (1.38 g, 10
mmol), stirred vigorously and heated (50-56 °C), treated with the
appropriate α-haloketone (4.2 mmol), held for 1-5 h with heating, stirred
vigorously (course of reaction monitored by TLC) and poured into H2SO4
solution (100 mL, 1 N). The resulting precipitate was filtered off and
crystallized from propanol-2. 7-(2-Oxopropoxy)-3-phenylchromen-2-one
(11). Yield 78%. mp 179-180 °C, C18H14O4. PMR spectrum (400 MHz, DMSO-d6,
δ, ppm, J/Hz): 2.18 (3H, s, CH3-3′′), 5.00 (2H, s, CH2-1′′), 6.98 (1H,
dd, J = 2.0, 8.0, H-6), 7.00 (1H, d, J = 2.0, H-8), 7.37-7.46 (3H, m,
H-3′, H-4′, H-5′), 7.67-7.71 (3H, m, H-5, H-2′, H-6′), 8.20 (1H, s, H-4).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
