$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 2,7-Di[4-(acryloyloxy
hexyloxy)phenyl]-9,9-di(n-octyl)fluorene (M2).
2,7-Di(4-hydroxyphenyl)-9,9-di(n-octyl)fluorene (137.0 mg, 0.24 mmol) was
synthesized according to previously published procedures.11,23 M1 (338.0
mg, 1.44 mmol), K2CO3 (66.0 mg, 0.48 mmol), a small amount of 18-crown-6
and solvent acetone (5 mL) were added to a 25 mL single-neck round-bottom
flask. The mixture was stirred and refluxed for 15 h, then cooled to room
temperature and the mixture was filtered. The crude product was
chromatographically purified on silica gel eluting with petroleum ether/
DCM (2/1, V/V), M2 as a yellowish solid (161.0 mg, 76%). Mp: 57.9°C. 1H
NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3, δ): 7.76 (d, J=7.8 Hz, 2H), 7.62 (d, J=8.4 Hz, 4H),
7.56 (d d, J=7.8 Hz, J=1.8 Hz, 2H), 7.54 (s, 2H), 7.02 (d, J=8.4 Hz, 4H),
6.44 (d d, J=17.4 Hz, J=1.2 Hz, 2H), 6.14-6.19 (m, 2H), 5.85 (d d, J=10.2
Hz, J=1.2 Hz, 2H), 4.22 (t, J=6.6 Hz, 4H), 4.06 (t, J=6.6 Hz, 4H),
2.06-2.03 (m, 4H), 1.90-1.85 (m, 4H), 1.79-1.74 (m, 4H), 1.61-1.56 (m,
4H), 1.54-1.49 (m, 4H), 1.23-1.09 (m, 20H), 0.83 (t, J=7.2 Hz, 6H),
0.77-0.72 (m, 4H) (In Supporting Information, Figure S2 is 1H NMR
spectrum of M2 in CDCl3.). 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3,δ): 166.35, 158.56,
151.58, 139.56, 134.19, 130.52, 128.62, 128.15, 125.53, 121.06, 119.82,
114.81, 67.92, 64.55, 55.18, 40.46, 31.78, 30.04, 29.21, 28.60, 25.80,
23.80, 22.59, 14.06 (In Supporting Information, Figure S3 is 13C NMR
spectrum of M2 in CDCl3.). High-resolution atmo spheric pressure-chemical
ionization Fourier-transform ion cyclotron resonance mass-spectroscopy
(HR-APCI-FT-ICR MS) revealed the parent ion peak at m/z=883.5873 (calcd
for C59H79O6: 883.5871, [M+H]+) (In Supporting Informa tion, Figure S4 is
HR-APCI-FT-ICR-MS spectrum of M2.).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of the water-soluble fluorene-containing fluorescent polymer
by one-pot method
