$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.2.1 Synthesis of Ethyl
α-(4-Alkylaryloxy)Tetradecanoate. Ethyl α-(4-alkylaryloxy)tetradecanoate
were synthesized in one-step reaction of 0.105 mol ethyl 2-bromomyristate
with 0.10 mol phenol (4-ethylphenol, 4-n-butylphenol, or 2-naphthol) in
60 mL dry dimethyl formamide (DMF) and 30 mL dry benzene. Excess
potassium carbonate (0.15 mol) was acted as acid accepter, and water was
extracted from the reaction system. The reaction mixture was extensively
stirred overnight at refluxing temperature, and then stopped by cooling
to room temperature. The inorganic salt was separated out by filtration,
and the remaining solid was washed with 100 mL petroleum ether. The
organic portion was collected and shifted to a separating funnel and was
extracted thrice with 100 mL water, and then dried over anhydrous
magnesium sulfate. The organic portion was evaporated in a rotary
evaporator. The crude products were distilled under reduced pressure. 1c
(Ar=C6H4, R=C4H9): yield, 72.5%. Reactant: 4-n-butylphenol. b.p., 242∼248
°C (0.80 mmHg); n20d, 1.4729; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz), δ 0.89 (t, 6H),
1.22∼1.54 (m, 28H), 1.55 (m, 2H), 1.90 (m, 2H), 2.53 (t, 2H), 4.21 (m,
2H), 4.54 (t, 1H), 6.78 (d, 2H), 7.05 (d, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Properties of Aromatic Side Chained N-Acyltaurate
Surfactants
